29. Website database recommendation

Store one row per server per completed week. Useful fields:

server_id
week_start
week_end
unique_players
join_sessions
guest_joins
new_players
returning_players
retained_players
previous_week_players
retention_percent
month_unique
year_unique
all_time_unique
all_time_joins
received_at

A unique constraint on:

server_id + week_start

prevents accidental duplicate weekly records when a webhook is retried.

30. Multi-server deployment

For several BeamMP servers on one Linux host, use separate directories:

/opt/beammp-server1/
/opt/beammp-server2/
/opt/beammp-server3/

Use separate ports, AuthKeys, ServerConfig files, Resources directories, PlayerCounter databases, webhook server identifiers, and service units.

Do not point two running PlayerCounter instances at the same stats.json or joins.csv.

31. Backups

Back up at least:

ServerConfig.toml
Resources/Client/
Resources/Server/
Resources/Server/PlayerCounter/data/stats.json
Resources/Server/PlayerCounter/data/joins.csv

Back up before BeamMP updates, plugin updates, map changes, large mod changes, manual JSON edits, or server migrations.

Linux example:

sudo systemctl stop beammp.service
sudo tar -czf \
  /var/backups/beammp-$(date +%Y-%m-%d).tar.gz \
  /opt/beammp
sudo systemctl start beammp.service

32. Updating BeamMP Server

Recommended procedure:

Announce maintenance.

Stop the server.

Back up the installation.

Download the current BeamMP Server binary.

Replace the old server executable unless the release notes require more changes.

Preserve ServerConfig.toml and Resources/.

Restore execute permission/ownership on Linux.

Start the server.

Check startup output and version.

Run playerstats and retention.

Test an external connection.

33. Updating PlayerCounter

Use this procedure:

1. Stop BeamMP
2. Back up Resources/Server/PlayerCounter/data/
3. Replace main.lua
4. Preserve stats.json
5. Preserve joins.csv
6. Start BeamMP
7. Review PlayerCounter console output
8. Run playerstats
9. Run retention

Do not delete the data folder during a normal upgrade.

34. Updating the webhook sender

1. Back up weekly_push.py
2. Replace/update the script
3. Verify webhook URL and secret configuration
4. Run it manually
5. Confirm HTTP 200
6. Confirm the correct website record
7. Verify the timer/task is still enabled

