36. Privacy recommendation

Keep individual BeamMP IDs and player-specific history on the game server. A public website normally only needs aggregated values such as:

Weekly unique players
Join sessions
New players
Returning players
Retention
Monthly unique players
Annual unique players
All-time unique players

Avoid publicly exposing raw stats.json, raw joins.csv, BeamMP IDs, player-specific join histories, or IP addresses.

37. Troubleshooting

Server does not appear in the public list
Check:
Private = false
Then verify the AuthKey, TCP/UDP reachability, Internet access, and startup log. Make sure the same AuthKey is not already being used by another running server.

Cannot direct-connect
Verify the IP, port, server process, TCP firewall rule, and UDP firewall rule. On the same PC use 127.0.0.1. On the LAN use the host's LAN IPv4.

TCP works but UDP fails
Recheck router UDP forwarding, Windows/Linux firewall, provider firewall, and the port in ServerConfig.toml.

Home hosting still fails
Investigate CGNAT. If your ISP does not provide reachable inbound IPv4, use a public IPv4, VPS, or game host.

PlayerCounter does not load

Verify the exact path:
Resources/Server/PlayerCounter/main.lua

Restart BeamMP and look for [PlayerCounter] messages.
/playerstats does nothing

Check:
local ALLOW_PLAYER_COMMANDS = true

Then test the server-console command:
playerstats

Reconnect does not increase unique players
That is intentional. One account reconnecting ten times is one unique player and ten join sessions.

Retention is N/A
This can be expected after a fresh install, migration from an older counter, or when the complete previous cohort is unavailable.

Weekly webhook fails
Run weekly_push.py manually and look for DNS, TLS, HTTP, JSON, or file-path errors.

HTTP 401
Check the webhook secret, HMAC implementation, signature header, and whether the website verifies the exact raw request body.

HTTP 404
Check WEBHOOK_URL, the site route, and reverse-proxy configuration.

HTTP 500
The request reached the website but the application failed. Review the website/application logs.

Linux BeamMP service fails
systemctl status beammp.service
journalctl -u beammp.service
Check the binary path, execute permission, WorkingDirectory, service user ownership, and ServerConfig.toml/Resources permissions.

--- Weekly timer does not run
systemctl status beammp-weekly-stats.timer
systemctl list-timers
sudo systemctl start beammp-weekly-stats.service
journalctl -u beammp-weekly-stats.service

